            {
                "entry_id": "cb19f538-d317-3ef4-af8f-3041428ebf3c",
                "word": "crocodilian",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "deac0843-f348-4bea-9088-af3f35ca1fe2",
                        "entry_id": "cb19f538-d317-3ef4-af8f-3041428ebf3c",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "crocodilians"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8fcd4787-f591-31a7-ad66-f7d035688068",
                        "entry_id": "cb19f538-d317-3ef4-af8f-3041428ebf3c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any reptile of the order Crocodilia; a crocodile, alligator, caiman or gavial."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4ef9f910-3015-408a-86dd-fcaa3b17620e",
                                "sense_id": "8fcd4787-f591-31a7-ad66-f7d035688068",
                                "text": "1989, Walter P. Coombs, Jr., Modern analogs for dinosaur nesting and parental behavior, James Orville Farlow (editor), Paleobiology of the Dinosaurs, Issue 238, page 47,\nMound-nesting crocodilians and megapodes appear to be indifferent to nest-site parameters, but susceptibility of crocodilian mound nests to predation or drowning may be altered by site selection."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d1c49488-9a5b-4996-bcb2-eef798ad73ae",
                                "sense_id": "8fcd4787-f591-31a7-ad66-f7d035688068",
                                "text": "Superb predators, the crocodilians are reptiles, and the only survivors of the archosaurs that included dinosaurs."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a24b6c04-e2ab-49a0-9a5c-9a01ba51107c",
                                "sense_id": "8fcd4787-f591-31a7-ad66-f7d035688068",
                                "text": "Crocodilians are essentially lizard-like in basic shape and are adapted to a largely aquatic life. ln water, they hunt and eat their prey and advertise their size and location by bellowing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "776264c5-7cea-49b2-81d9-c695322b3202",
                                "sense_id": "8fcd4787-f591-31a7-ad66-f7d035688068",
                                "text": "However, it is possible that baby titanoboas and Titanoboa eggs were preyed upon by the same crocodilians the adults ate."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "498e2250-7d8c-4f06-92e6-42cc151f00c8",
                        "source_entry_id": "cb19f538-d317-3ef4-af8f-3041428ebf3c",
                        "source_sense_id": "8fcd4787-f591-31a7-ad66-f7d035688068",
                        "source_sense_description": "reptiles",
                        "target_lang_word": "crocodilien",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "crocodilien",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "facdbf42-e6cb-3d53-8b91-d778d0631fe4",
                                        "entry_id": "a6a6176d-44af-3916-9650-a6a10c1fc09f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Semblable aux crocodiles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9e169e27-1d45-4b1b-8285-7c64a3a94e5d",
                                                "sense_id": "facdbf42-e6cb-3d53-8b91-d778d0631fe4",
                                                "text": "Le gavial est un reptile crocodilien de la famille des gavialidés au museau mince et allongé qui vit en Inde."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "crocodilien",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73db1768-01b8-38bc-9715-e7754d20e710",
                                        "entry_id": "a760873f-955d-3389-b3a1-90d9c95d8242",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Reptile de l’ordre Crocodilia : crocodile, alligator ou gavial."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee023f51-3f45-4537-ad28-4e8895fbe675",
                                                "sense_id": "73db1768-01b8-38bc-9715-e7754d20e710",
                                                "text": "Aux côtés des nombreux restes de poissons littoraux, les tétrapodes sont représentés par des chéloniens, crocodiliens, ophidiens, plésiosaures, ptérosaures et dinosaures."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d04f3ca2-ea0d-4d20-a09b-15a3b9525851",
                                                "sense_id": "73db1768-01b8-38bc-9715-e7754d20e710",
                                                "text": "Dans ces étendues d’eau vivait un prédateur plus gros que lui, un crocodilien de plus de quinze mètres connu sous le nom de deinosuchus, le seul animal capable de tuer un T-Rex pour peu qu’il se soit aventuré trop près de l’eau à la recherche d’une proie."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
